@startuml activity-access
title Activity diagram: getting in with an institutional email

|Student|
start
:Enter institutional email;
|Ayni|
if (A university claims the email domain?) then (no)
  :Answer that the institution\nis not affiliated;
  |Student|
  stop
else (yes)
endif
|Ayni|
:Create single use access link\n(token stored hashed, expires in minutes);
:Publish AccessRequested;
|Email Service|
:Deliver the link;
|Student|
:Open the link;
|Ayni|
if (Link valid, unexpired and unused?) then (no)
  :Reject and offer a new link;
  |Student|
  stop
else (yes)
endif
|Ayni|
:Consume the link and open a long lived session;
if (First entry?) then (yes)
  |University Academic System|
  :Return name, career, term,\napproved courses and grades;
  |Ayni|
  :Activate student;
  :Publish StudentActivated;
  fork
    :wallet grants the university's credits;
  fork again
    :skills enables courses\nthe grades already justify;
  end fork
  :Resume onboarding from the last step;
else (no)
endif
|Student|
:Use the platform;
stop
@enduml
